{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>A woman with whom a man lies.</b> Scripture did not write 'a man when he lies with a woman,' for it testifies concerning the woman that she does not become impure on account of any emission whatsoever other than a blood flow or a seminal emission, just as impurity occurs in the man. However, the woman's impurity through seminal emission occurs only when a man lies with her, even though it is in the hidden place."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:24.381285871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}